  "body": "### What is the issue with the HTML Standard?\n\nThe popover implicit anchor is cleared _after_ the `beforetoggle` event when hiding, whereas the invoker is cleared _before_. When showing, they're set at the same moment. This makes almost identical but slightly different, which is slightly annoying for implementation purposes. I could also see this being confusing for developers as well if they use the `beforetoggle` event to prevent hiding and the invoker gets unlinked, but not the anchoring.\n\nI don't have a strong opinion whether both should happen before or after the `beforetoggle` event, but it seems like it should be consistent. I think there was probably an intentional reason for the popover implicit anchor to be cleared after, so I'd probably suggest that.\n\ncc @josepharhar @mfreed7 @annevk ",
